son Ford  now the director has said Harrison Ford  is not really gonna be a co-lead in this  he will be there he will be featured but  he's not gonna be featured too heavily  would you my mind good I think that it's  the better way to end the directors also  said they won't definitively answer the  is Deckard a replica question which on  one hand good I don't think that ever  should be as definitively on the other  hand I'm like well you're gonna have to  integrate some new information about  replicants because by what we know when  the fact they're supposed to have a four  year lifespan the very fact that he's  still alive would normally answer that  question one way or the other so they're  gonna have to find a way to fudge that a  little bit but in general premise not  answering that question dude that's the  way to go it's also fairly going to be  rated R which I'm happy about and with  this director I'm fairly confident just  means that they will be free to explore  and bring in the violence as is  necessary not that it's going to be like  Deadpool and just revel in its already  not that there's anything wrong with  doing that but that's not what Blade  Runner is and the few glimpses we get of  the city look really consistent with  with the blade runner world that we know  which is good um I think probably as  long as you don't think too hard about  it because if this is basically as much  time has passed in the movie world that  has passed in the real world um  technology's changed a lot here since  the 80s so you'd think a similar amount  of time passing things would have  advanced but at the same time I don't  want them to because I want that same  world again so it becomes a case where  potentially the aesthetic and the  narrative might not totally gel we'll  see we'll see if it's something that  gets addressed or if they just hope you  roll with it and and maybe if they do it  well enough I will just roll with it and  it'll be fine again personally for me  the most comforting thing was just the  little bits of music especially at the  very end of that teaser it was Blade  Runner music cuz that soundtrack nothing  else sounds like that soundtrack it is  so gorgeous and so perfect and so unique  and I think  nobody else really tries to make  something sound like that because only  Blade Runner sounds like that only blade  runner looks like that only blade runner  feels like that and and if they can  recapture that and I think there's a  chance they can I'm reserving a little  bit of my anticipation but between what  I'm seeing what I'm hearing and what I'm  reading in terms of the mindset of the  director this could work and I would  really really really like it too so  that's sort of where I am right now with  blade runner 2049 have you seen this  teaser have you been reading the  interviews what's your thoughts on all  of this whatever they are drop something  down in the comments and let's talk  about it don't forget to Like subscribe  check me out on Twitter at Council of  geeks give a listen to the counsel of  geeks podcast available on iTunes and  stitcher and until next time this  council is adjourned
 

